{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: Boot-failure warning bypasses the injectable output seam**

`_prepareAsyncPool` reports the degraded boot with a direct `stderr.writeln`:

```dart
    } catch (e) {
      stderr.writeln('dmtools: engine-worker pool boot failed '
          '(runAsync will report an error on first use): $e');
    }
```

`stderr` is the right channel for a CLI diagnostic (it keeps the stdout run result machine-parseable), but every other output of `CliDispatcher` goes through the injectable `_writer` seam — this is the one line a test cannot observe, so the new `cli_dispatcher_pool_boot_test.dart` suite asserts the degrade path only via the JS-side `not booted` error and can never assert the warning itself was emitted.

If you want the warning covered too, mirror the `writer` pattern, e.g.:

```dart
CliDispatcher({
  void Function(String line)? writer,
  void Function(String line)? errorWriter, // defaults to stderr.writeln
  ...
```

…and assert `errorLines` in the boot-failure test. Fine to defer; the functional behavior (no bricking, clear JS error) is already tested.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1_stderr_seam.md"}

